sumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Pogo11cSguR0JcD9UXApNYdIUwBIq3HApgNswkXJL3gƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka0ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ByNi5f4n1JZ5zIxPpEkEmvcUrzKAnEMpLuh4j71yrj8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka0ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;zfNa1w923k-aHklSRp7vrhTRd68Tn2Byz1wiaMBU2CEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkhstandardƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;CoN9e-FSTOZMmoNtMrvl6jY0GZm4qtMjbRPcO6ppkcEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkhstandardƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;mFLDNh_tA1vrnFBa-43ZK4VaqHQyON5GPTXPHnXRLbMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx$146f05d4-34eb-4815-87f9-a1a4cb846bf7ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;wU7JuPoOR0ATm5kxP4s_N62p6A6ASedettHMuv2eTdAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky%á{"tool":"submit_revision_request","failureLayer":"writer-model","replayFrom":"writer-model","summary":"Two bounded prose repairs and one editorial-surface repair are required before publication. The writer model omitted FIFA's prior on-record statement about climate-risk managementâ€”present in the sourceâ€”leaving the institutional-criticism claim without the subject's available voice. The writer model also produced two near-duplicate sentences in the opening paragraph that both contextualize the same smoke/AQI event, which the deterministic copy-edited gate flagged. The raw SEO query string in the tags field is a carrier artifact that repair_editorial_surfaces will prune.","requiredRepairs":["Add FIFA's prior general statement on climate-risk management â€” documented in the source but omitted by the writer model â€” before the paragraph noting that no comment was returned. Without it the piece criticizes FIFA for lacking a plan while suppressing the organization's own characterization of its approach.","Consolidate the two near-duplicate sentences in the opening paragraph that both describe Canadian wildfire smoke blanketing the region and the resulting AQI levels. The deterministic gate flagged them; they repeat the same geographic and hazard framing within three sentences.","Run repair_editorial_surfaces to remove the raw SEO query string from the tags field and regenerate summary and description from the admitted body."],"repairTools":[{"tool":"replace_exact_body_text","before":"Large swaths of the United States, including the Midwest and the East Coast, have been blanketed by smoke from Canadian wildfires, forcing cities to confront hazardous air quality [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). While the air quality index in the region climbed to unhealthy levels on Thursday, triggering state alerts, the governing body for the tournament has not yet detailed a contingency plan for the event [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).","after":"Wildfire smoke blowing from Canada has blanketed large swaths of the Midwest and East Coast, with the air quality index in the region climbing to unhealthy and very unhealthy levels on Thursday and triggering state alerts. Despite the hazard, the tournament's governing body has not detailed a contingency plan for the event [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/)."},{"tool":"replace_exact_body_text","before":"Neither FIFA nor New York City Department of Health officials immediately responded to Grist's request for comment [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).","after":"In a previous statement to Grist, FIFA said that \"climate-related risks are assessed as part of overall tournament planning and managed in close coordination with host cities, stadium authorities, and national agencies,\" but did not address wildfire smoke or air quality thresholds. Neither FIFA nor New York City Department of Health officials immediately responded to Grist's request for further comment [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/)."},{"tool":"repair_editorial_surfaces"}],"report":"## Editorial Assessment â€” reporting-source-1-for-wildfire-smoke-threatens-cup-final\n\n### Pipeline Diagnosis\n\nFailure layer is writer-model. The single source (Grist, 2026-07-17) is adequate in scope for a summary-and-reaction piece on this topic. The assignment is well-formed and the search terms map cleanly to the available evidence. The deterministic standards mark the manuscript publishable=true at the packet level, and the gates_clear=false frontmatter state reflects outstanding editorial work, not a hard rejection. All defects identified below are local and repair-tractable.\n\n### Source and Attribution Audit\n\nAll material factual claims in the body are traceable to the single witnessed source: the Grist article published 2026-07-17. Attribution is visible in the form of inline hyperlinks on every sentence, which is noisy but not factually misleading. Named quotes are correctly attributed â€” Dr. Courtney Howard's statement is properly passed through to the Associated Press rather than claimed as direct reporting, and Nicholas Watanabe is identified with institution and title matching the source.\n\nThe research packet flags primary-source-unproven as a warning: no primary records (AQI data feeds, FIFA policy documents, NWSL policy text) are in the packet; every claim flows through Grist's journalism. This limitation is inherent to the source layer and does not require replay, but a production note is warranted if the outlet has a secondary-sourcing disclosure policy.\n\n### Fairness Gap â€” FIFA's Prior Statement (Material; Bounded Repair)\n\nThe manuscript criticizes FIFA for lacking an air quality policy and notes that Grist's request for comment went unanswered. The witnessed source, however, documents a prior FIFA statement to Grist: \"Climate-related risks are assessed as part of overall tournament planning and managed in close coordination with host cities, stadium authorities, and national agencies.\" The writer model omitted this statement. Its omission leaves the piece criticizing an institution while suppressing the institution's only documented voice in the evidence record. This meets the fairness standard trigger: consequential allegation, documented opportunity to be heard (and a response on record), response not represented. The repair inserts the prior statement with accurate framing that it addressed general climate risks but not smoke or AQI thresholds specifically.\n\n### Near-Duplicate Redundancy â€” Opening Paragraph (Moderate; Bounded Repair)\n\nThe deterministic copy-edited gate issued eleven near-duplicate-proximity warnings. Most of the flagged pairs, on inspection, cover distinct angles (e.g., the athlete health quote versus the vulnerable-populations sentence; the NWSL policy sentence versus the no-comment sentence). However, the opening paragraph presents a genuine redundancy: three sentences in sequence all frame the same contextual fact â€” Canadian wildfire smoke is blanketing the region and creating hazardous AQI near New York City â€” before the piece turns to the FIFA preparedness question. Sentences two and three in particular repeat the same geographic and hazard framing within a single paragraph. The repair merges them into one specific sentence, improving information density without losing any evidentiary content.\n\n### Missing Demand-Lens H2 (Warning; Not Blocking)\n\nThe deterministic standards flag a missing H2 that would naturally signal the demand lens. Given the article structure â€” a three-section piece with \"A Gap in Institutional Preparedness,\" \"Risks to Human Performance and Health,\" and \"Watching the Atmosphere\" â€” this warning reflects that reader-demand framing (e.g., what fans, players, or local residents can do or should know) is absent rather than that a specific heading is required. This is a structural note for the writer rather than a blocking repair at this stage, since the source does not provide demand-side guidance material beyond the generic \"avoid spending time outdoors\" official advisory already captured.\n\n### Carrier Artifacts (Editorial Surfaces)\n\nThe tags field contains the raw SEO query string \"wildfire smoke threatens cup final fifa doesn plan\" as a literal tag value. This is a carrier artifact from the research packet intake that was not converted to natural language tags. repair_editorial_surfaces will prune this and regenerate summary and description from the admitted body, resolving that surface without manual prose intervention.\n\n### Headline and Lede Fidelity\n\nThe headline \"FIFA Lacks Air Quality Policy as Wildfire Smoke Approaches World Cup Final\" is faithful to the source claim and appropriately hedged â€” it asserts an observable absence (no documented policy) rather than a proven causal chain. The lede matches the headline and introduces the open-air stadium detail from the source, which grounds the threat in a physical constraint. No sensationalism, no claim strengthening beyond what the source warrants.\n\n### Stale Temporal Framing\n\nThe manuscript is dated 2026-07-20 (the day of the final itself) but the source article was published 2026-07-17. The manuscript uses the source's \"as of Friday morning\" language to describe AQI conditions that are now three days stale relative to the manuscript date. This is inherent to the single-source limit and not independently repairable without additional current sources. The editor should consider whether a dateline note or a qualifier (\"as of Friday, July 18\") would flag the temporal gap for readers encountering the piece on match day.\n\n### Summary\n\nThree bounded repairs â€” consolidating the redundant AQI sentences in the opening, inserting FIFA's omitted prior statement, and running repair_editorial_surfaces on carrier artifacts â€” are sufficient to clear the manuscript for publication. No replay is required."}ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Dl3Me6NY8f0TeG8mNsCAc4S4FV69MQdDonUkVcFKyB8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;m4GPaaPr50YBrvXw8PumtmigwHViSd8URl0BNEyLJyUƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;tDicZlouYgUeYMVydGlEZsdnn6CDfEZ2ooZnohKYfSAƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;DTDPNWlXCSsq-bA0K4HTifrH-aMSNEMYbkZidfsZ5ogƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxclaude-code-cli-invocationsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;-30O3hyWP-hfY2L2s75LJOTSuV0iiswtDx2JRHEgV40ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka1ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;FcKTykhKwFSjuZM2vVITDkxcvTNFWZTztFnrH6QWe_8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒer